NAME
    uniq - drop adjacent repeated lines

SYNOPSIS
    uniq [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the files named (as one stream; globs expand, "-" is stdin),
    or stdin, leaving out every line that equals the line before it.
    Only adjacent repeats go: sort first to drop every repeat. Each file
    ends a line. uniq is /BIN/UNIQ. stdin is the shell's < file or pipe
    (see shell), else the console up to Ctrl-D.

LIMITS
    Lines are cut at 255 characters (CR is dropped).

EXAMPLES
    uniq /FRUIT.TXT      the second "banana 12 yellow" goes; the
                         second "apple 3 red" stays (not adjacent)

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: input from a pipe (sort f | uniq).
    New: several files, globs and "-".
    Ported from P8X os/commands/uniq.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    sort, wc, rdline
